2026-10-05 Kumar <kumar@nabu>
	* 6.18.55-4:
	- Display: Drop the dpu_kms_hw_init loop that clears every INTF_TIMING_ENGINE_EN
	  register before the IOMMU is attached. It was added to stop bootloader left-over
	  DMA causing SMMU faults, but it also blanks the DSI interfaces that the firmware
	  handed over mid-boot, which shows up as a grey half and vertical lines across the
	  other half. 6.16 has no such loop and displays correctly, so match it and see
	  whether the panel fault is from this loop or from upstream 6.18 DSI code.
	- Package: Bump pkgrel

2026-10-05 Kumar <kumar@nabu>
	* 6.18.55-3:
	- Display: Remove the 90 degree panel rotation from the nabu panel node. The NT36523
	  panel's native mode is already portrait 1600x2560, so the rotation property made DRM
	  disagree with the DSI timings on the sync-dual-DSI link and produced a vertical seam
	  with a grey half. This matches 6.16, which has no rotation and works correctly.
	- Package: Bump pkgrel and retarget the source at this branch

2026-10-05 Kumar <kumar@nabu>
	* 6.18.55-2:
	- Display: Fix DSI PLL lock failure on boot by removing CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE from disp_cc_mdss_pclk0_clk_src and pclk1
	- DSI PHY: Restore PM runtime resume in dsi_phy_driver_probe to keep iface clock running during early PLL registration
	- DSI PLL 7nm: Prevent premature PLL bias disable in vco_set_rate during mode set and live UEFI handover
	- Package: Update package release and include changelog

2026-10-04 Kumar <kumar@nabu>
	* 6.18.55-1:
	- Baseline: Initial release of Linux 6.18.55 for Xiaomi Pad 5 (nabu)
	- UFS: Add DT frequency table and reset quirk for Samsung UFS compatibility
	- FastRPC SLPI: Enable high-IOVA alias mapping and sensor PDR domain registration
	- Camera: Support OV13B10 rear, OV8856 front, and CN3927 autofocus
	- Audio: SM8150 machine driver with 24-bit microphone capture and speaker routing
	- Power: PM8150B SMB5 charger driver and USB-PD sink support
	- Touch & Stylus: Novatek NT36523 touchscreen and IDTP9418 wireless pen charging
